{"data": [{"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-01T16:47:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116935154136461775"], "id": "2116935154136461775", "in_reply_to_user_id": "17974586", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15438, "like_count": 12, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@willystaley What’s the word on kombucha?", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116935154136461775"}, {"author_id": "188369814", "created_at": "2026-11-01T16:43:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116934214335520777"], "id": "2116934214335520777", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 97, "impression_count": 45131, "like_count": 261, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 47, "retweet_count": 21}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116887789790982346", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Where AI stands after Friday.\n\nThe 7th-largest sell-off in the last two years, after rallying over 500% since ChatGPT's November 2022 release.\n\nAlso note, the all-time high was October 6, less than a month ago. https://t.co/xyDCt0CPIL https://t.co/zUah14Igs9", "url": "https://x.com/biancoresearch/status/2116934214335520777"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-01T16:21:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116928596497633755"], "id": "2116928596497633755", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3555, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "1/ RIP Bill Nordhaus.\n\nWhen I was a grad student at Yale in the 00s a lot of the old school giants were still there.  James Tobin still occasionally came to seminars!", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116928596497633755"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-01T16:14:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116926765050511811"], "id": "2116926765050511811", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 4517, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116243133956796806", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This is great!  Hooray for Claude https://t.co/tjcY9C1LmR", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116926765050511811"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-01T15:44:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116919329312895340"], "id": "2116919329312895340", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 113, "impression_count": 71409, "like_count": 837, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 39, "retweet_count": 17}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116918488677658728", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "My $0.02\n\n1) The rationalist/EA world has had far better intuitions about AI than the vast majority of the public for a very long time.\n\n2) Anyone who's been practicing their argument for years WILL beat you in an argument, but that's distinct from them actually being right. https://t.co/EHxAbtOTee", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116919329312895340"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-01T15:36:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116917361790116216"], "id": "2116917361790116216", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 16046, "like_count": 50, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116913837006004679", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Funny the whole reason I was thinking about this is that I just watched the Sopranos episode where they made a big deal of Hunter Scangarelo getting accepted early to Reed College. https://t.co/PQ5yDO55x8", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116917361790116216"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-01T15:31:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116916008145305785"], "id": "2116916008145305785", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 20162, "like_count": 287, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "NYC marathon day. Best of luck to all the sign-holders. Hope yours goes viral.", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116916008145305785"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-11-01T15:29:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116915439024455977"], "id": "2116915439024455977", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2603, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "\"Established truckmakers can slow #China’s relentless export push by pitching customers on their extensive repair &amp; maintenance networks, said the head of a Toyota-backed heavy-duty vehicles producer\"\nhttps://t.co/P7T48vJuV2", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2116915439024455977"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-01T14:57:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116907552336400466"], "id": "2116907552336400466", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 79, "impression_count": 56245, "like_count": 411, "quote_count": 14, "reply_count": 39, "retweet_count": 16}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116666792814989585", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This post says the AI safety movement is becoming a scene where people compete to out-doom each other, and sound overly pessimistic, when in fact some highly respected forecasters think the odds of humanity surviving could be anywhere from 10-40%. https://t.co/r92jZ7q7xV", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116907552336400466"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-01T14:49:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116905349672538289"], "id": "2116905349672538289", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2293, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "At 9 AM PT on Friday November 6th, me &amp; the ONE AND ONLY @keds_economist will be doing our usual fun BLS chit-chat.\n\nKathryn Anne started a tradition of exotic locations, last week was DC and I bet you can't wait to find out where she'll be on Friday!\n\nhttps://t.co/6F5QbNHiRe", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116905349672538289"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-01T14:43:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116903940520604007"], "id": "2116903940520604007", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4730, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "It’s Ruby-crowned kinglet season!", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116903940520604007"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-01T14:24:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116899185631064544"], "id": "2116899185631064544", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 243, "impression_count": 68634, "like_count": 2667, "quote_count": 11, "reply_count": 52, "retweet_count": 101}, "text": "Roddenberry’s rule was absolutely bananas and one of the reasons TNG ended up being a good show is that the writers ended up circumventing it a lot https://t.co/vo3xLaVx8Q", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116899185631064544"}, {"author_id": "188369814", "created_at": "2026-11-01T13:39:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116887789790982346"], "id": "2116887789790982346", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 327, "impression_count": 186566, "like_count": 1264, "quote_count": 15, "reply_count": 80, "retweet_count": 105}, "text": "Where the stock market stands after Friday. https://t.co/W1xlMBPC8L", "url": "https://x.com/biancoresearch/status/2116887789790982346"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-11-01T11:24:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116853760139903172"], "id": "2116853760139903172", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 139, "impression_count": 32495, "like_count": 225, "quote_count": 6, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 43}, "text": "I recently cited Sven Beckert's very good book on the history of cotton production in which he argued that capitalism and globalization occurred together. In this interview he argues that the issue today is no longer the problem of production, which has historically always been", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2116853760139903172"}, {"author_id": "30034124", "created_at": "2026-11-01T08:48:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116814503782281685"], "id": "2116814503782281685", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 3436, "like_count": 77, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 14}, "text": "As Fermilab builds components for its powerful new linear accelerator, engineers are driving innovation by using a collaborative robot to automate the assembly of superconducting cavities, sharply reducing the risk of errors in a cleanroom environment.\nhttps://t.co/sw0sOGL5G2", "url": "https://x.com/Fermilab/status/2116814503782281685"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-11-01T05:26:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116763782269514010"], "id": "2116763782269514010", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 16804, "like_count": 98, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 17}, "text": "Caixin: \"China’s electric two-wheeler exports rose nearly 38% to $7.3 billion in the first nine months of 2026, led by strong growth in Latin America and Africa as manufacturers sought to offset declining domestic sales. Sales in China fell 4.8% to 48.4 million units in the first", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2116763782269514010"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-11-01T05:18:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116761852679975252"], "id": "2116761852679975252", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 51, "impression_count": 18500, "like_count": 176, "quote_count": 6, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 35}, "text": "SCMP: \"China is further narrowing access to a key government recruitment programme for overseas-educated graduates, limiting their pathways into the country’s civil service and party-state system.\"\nhttps://t.co/UYs6W6sgFK", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2116761852679975252"}, {"author_id": "